# Changelog

## 1.0.0 (unreleased)

DRAFT — finalize this heading (add the release date, drop "unreleased") when
the 1.0.0 release is cut. Note: 0.9.12 on PyPI dates from 2020-01-18 and
predates everything below.

### Changed
- Modernized to Python 3.11-3.13, numpy 2, and pandas 3
- Python 3.10 is no longer supported (it reached end of life in October 2026)
- Python 3.14 is best effort for 1.0: detk is expected to install and run
  on it, but it is not tested in CI or listed in the classifiers, and 1.0
  promises only the versions CI tests
- New toolchain: `pyproject.toml` with the hatchling build backend, uv for
  environment/dependency management, ruff for lint and formatting
- Documentation moved to MkDocs Material, published on GitHub Pages at
  https://bu-neuromics.github.io/de_toolkit/
- Report frontend rebuilt on vendored Vega-Lite, removing the Highcharts
  licensing conflict; every module now has report views
- Snakemake removed from the internal machinery
- Many latent bug fixes, including: FLGCounts params were never recorded,
  FPKM report emission was unserializable, and shadowed tests were revived;
  `detk-norm library` and `detk-norm fpkm` failed on every CLI run (the
  library command was handed the count object, the lengths file was read as
  a table) and now run
- Feature IDs in a counts file, and sample names in a sample-info file, are
  read as text exactly as written, so a zero-padded ID such as `007` is no
  longer read as the number 7: it matches a lengths or mapping file that
  writes `007`, and every command writes it back as `007` (#48). This holds
  through R too: `detk-de deseq2` and `firth` and `detk-transform vst` and
  `rlog` read the IDs and sample names as text in R and wrapr reads R's
  output back the same way, so `007` and sample names such as `001` are
  kept, `detk-de deseq2` no longer stops on `001`-style sample names, and
  all-numeric versioned IDs such as `1.10` and `1.1` no longer collapse to
  one duplicate row name; `detk-enrich fgsea` reads the result's ID column
  as text, so `007` matches `007` in the GMT file, and `detk-util
  tidy-counts` and `tidy-covs` match `001`-style sample names, where they
  used to exit 1 (#67, DETK-0015). For R scripts run through
  `de_toolkit.wrapr`, the `output` and `metadata_out` tables are indexed by
  their first column read as text (they were typed by pandas), and the
  script can call `read.id.csv(fn, row.names=TRUE)` to read the counts or
  metadata with the IDs as text. The IDs are kept exactly as written,
  including whitespace: `" 007"` stays `" 007"`, where it used to become 7
  (text IDs always kept it)
- `de_toolkit.transform.rlog(count_obj, blind=False)`, rlog with a design,
  works: it passed the counts and an intercept column to DESeq2, which adds
  its own intercept, and failed in R ("not full rank"); it now drops both,
  as `detk-de deseq2` does. The command line cannot reach it yet:
  `detk-transform rlog --blind` passes its value to R as text, where DESeq2
  stops; leave `--blind` out for a blind rlog
- FPKM values change from 0.9.x: FPKM is now
  `count * 1e9 / (length * library size)` as documented, where 0.9.x computed
  `count / (1e6 * length)` and never divided by library size. In 0.9.x the
  wrong values reached users through the Python function
  `de_toolkit.norm.fpkm()`; the `detk-norm fpkm` command failed outright. This is a
  correction. `fpkm` now also refuses missing, zero and negative lengths, as
  `tpm` does

### Added
- Versioned module JSON schema for report data
- Process Run Crate (RO-Crate) provenance for CLI runs
- `detk-norm cpm` (counts per million) and `detk-norm tpm` (transcripts per
  million, from the same lengths file as `fpkm`), each with a report view.
  The lengths file (for `tpm` and `fpkm`) may start with a header line, which
  is recognized only when its length field is text other than a missing-value
  token such as `NA`; a feature listed twice is refused; feature IDs are
  matched as text, so numeric IDs work; `tpm` and `fpkm` require every length
  to be a positive number
- `detk-util annotate`: join feature metadata such as gene symbols onto a
  result table from a user-supplied mapping file, with `--strip-versions`
  for Ensembl version suffixes and a report of mapped and unmapped IDs (#29)
- Agent skill `detk` under `skills/`, installable with
  `npx skills add BU-Neuromics/de_toolkit`, and its docs page. It covers the
  1.0 commands: `detk-util gather` from quantifier outputs, `detk-norm`
  `deseq2`, `cpm`, `tpm`, `fpkm` and `library`, and `detk-util annotate` for
  gene symbols (#62)
- `detk-util gather`: combine per-sample salmon, kallisto, htseq-count or
  featureCounts outputs into a counts matrix, with the format detected from
  each file's header, sample names from the paths (or `--name-from`), an
  error when the samples list different features (`--on-mismatch=fill` or
  `drop` to go on) and a report of what was joined; it replaces csvgather in
  the documented workflow (#25)

### Fixed
- The report embeds its module JSON with `<`, `>` and `&` escaped, so a
  feature ID, sample name or annotation value containing `</script>` no
  longer breaks the report or injects markup; object keys (such as sample
  names) holding a quote or backslash no longer make the payload invalid
  JSON (#46)
- The report page shows every view's text as text: a filter command, DE
  term names, annotation and gather notes, a chart error, and an unknown
  module's name (in its card title, link, anchor and "Show data" button) are
  no longer inserted as markup by the page. Only the static SVG chart for
  very large point sets is inserted as markup. The charts' tooltips are
  written as text too: vega-embed's default tooltip wrote them as HTML and
  turned a field named `image` into an image, so a covariate column named
  `image` in a PCA chart could run script on hover. The charts' menu no longer offers
  "View Source", "View Compiled Vega" or "Open in Vega Editor": the first two
  wrote the chart's data, sample names included, unescaped into a new page
  of the report's origin, and the last sent it to an outside site. "Save as
  SVG" and "Save as PNG" remain, and "Show data" shows each module's JSON.
  An unknown module named like a chart (`pca-vis`) or like one of the
  page's own elements (`main`, `nav`, `vg-tooltip-element`, ...) no longer
  shares that element's id (#65)
- A one-column input file, such as a bare list of IDs, is read as one
  column; the delimiter sniffer no longer splits it on a letter of its
  header (`gene_id` became `g`, `n`, `_id`). The delimiter of every sniffed
  input (counts and column data, `detk-util annotate`, `tidy`,
  `tidy-counts`, `tidy-covs`, `detk-enrich fgsea` results) is now one of
  comma, tab, semicolon, pipe or space, taken from the first line, with
  space used only when no other splits it (a pipe table with a space in a
  header, such as a BioMart export, is no longer split on the spaces). A
  URL input is fetched once (#47)

